Atlas overlay patch 0004: privacy/crash-reporting-default-off
Why: crash reports stay on the machine. The crash reporting mode (Local State) is registered as
"disabled" instead of "ask", and an invalid stored value resets to "disabled" too; the person can
still choose "ask" or "automatic" in settings. Upload consent was already off until a choice is
made; this removes the prompt and the default path to the inherited project's crash host
(patches-0 P-03, crash part; the registration is in browser_prefs.cc, not in the crash reporting
file as patches-0 assumed).
Files: chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc, chrome/browser/crash_upload_list/helium_crash_reporting.cc
Test filter: *CrashReporting*; Local State of a new profile holds mode -1; zero-egress test (AT-7)
Rebase risk: M (five inherited patches edit browser_prefs.cc; the crash file is the inherited series' own)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series adds or patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc
@@ -1536,7 +1536,7 @@
   BrowserProcessImpl::RegisterPrefs(registry);
   registry->RegisterIntegerPref(
       prefs::kHeliumCrashReportingMode,
-      static_cast<int>(helium::CrashReportingMode::kAsk));
+      static_cast<int>(helium::CrashReportingMode::kDisabled));
   ChromeContentBrowserClient::RegisterLocalStatePrefs(registry);
 #if BUILDFLAG(CHROME_FOR_TESTING)
   chrome_for_testing::RegisterPrefs(registry);
